        "applicable": true,
        "evidence_summary": "Students use multiple phrasings: \"یہ سرکل ہے.\" (\"This is a circle.\") and later \"جو کلر کیا ہوا ہے...\" (\"The coloured part is on top...\") showing conceptual variety."
      },
      {
        "id": "D2",
        "name": "Student Reasoning in Responses",
        "score": 2,
        "evidence": "At least one student gives a reasoned explanation: [02:14] student explains subtraction reasoning \"10 میں سے 9، 9، 10 میں سے 1 گئے تو 9 بچ گیا۔\" (\"Out of 10, 9 gone so 9 remained.\") This answer follows a teacher prompt but contains internal reasoning about counts/parts.",
        "timestamp": "02:14",
        "applicable": true,
        "evidence_summary": "A student explains reasoning about counts: \"10 میں سے 9... تو 9 بچ گیا.\" (\"Out of 10, 9 gone so 9 remained.\") — a prompted but clear explanatory response."
      },
      {
        "id": "D3",
        "name": "Student-Initiated Questions",
        "score": 1,
        "evidence": "Students ask procedural questions but not content ones. Examples are procedural: [13:01] student: \"ٹیسٹ لکھیں؟\" (\"Write the test?\") and [14:58] student: \"اس کا سائز ہوگا؟\" (\"Will this have a size?\"). There are no student-initiated conceptual questions about fractions in the transcript.",
        "timestamp": "13:01 / 14:58",
        "applicable": true,
        "evidence_summary": "Students ask procedural questions like \"ٹیسٹ لکھیں؟\" (\"Write the test?\") and \"اس کا سائز ہوگا؟\" (\"Will this have a size?\") but no content questions."
      },
      {
        "id": "D4",
        "name": "Spontaneous Transfer & Connection-Making",
        "score": 2,
        "evidence": "A student offers a life-connection: after teacher's cake prompt, [03:27] student volunteers \"میں اپنے چھوٹے بھائی کی برتھ ڈے ہے.\" (\"It's my younger brother's birthday.\")—a genuine link from lesson to the student's life. The connection was prompted by the teacher's cake example, and the student supplied a real-world instance.",
        "timestamp": "03:27",
        "applicable": true,
        "evidence_summary": "Student links lesson to personal life: \"میں اپنے چھوٹے بھائی کی برتھ ڈے ہے.\" (\"My younger brother's birthday\"), prompted by the cake example but offered by the student."
      },
      {
        "id": "D5",
        "name": "Visible Learning Progression Across the Lesson",
        "score": 2,
        "evidence": "Student utterances progress from short labels to longer, vocabulary-rich explanations. Early: [00:34] student \"یہ سرکل ہے.\" (\"This is a circle.\"). Late: [08:44] student explains fraction parts: \"جو کلر کیا ہوا ہے، وہ اوپر ہے، اور ٹوٹل نیچے ہے.\" (\"The coloured part is on top and the total is below.\"). This shows increased length and use of key vocabulary.",
        "timestamp": "00:34 / 08:44",
        "applicable": true,
